WEBVTT

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.015
Twice a day, weather balloons rise from hundreds of stations around the world.

00:00:44.215 --> 00:00:48.988
This one swells as the air thins, until it is as wide as a small house.

00:00:49.188 --> 00:00:54.259
At thirty-five kilometres, the sky above is black, and the Earth below is curved.

00:00:54.459 --> 00:00:58.635
Then the balloon bursts, and its instruments drift home on a parachute.

